    "message": {
      "content": "# Validation Checklist for Multi-Node Language-Model Serving Systems\n\n## Purpose and Scope\n\nThis checklist validates that a distributed LLM serving system (tensor-parallel, pipeline-parallel, expert-parallel, or data-parallel deployments) behaves correctly under controlled conditions. It is designed to produce evidence that can survive audit, not merely to produce a passing score. Each item specifies what to check, how to check it, and what evidence to retain.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Configuration Identity\n\n**Goal:** Prove that every node in the cluster is running the exact same logical configuration, and that the configuration tested is the configuration reported.\n\n### 1.1 Model artifact identity\n- [ ] Record SHA-256 (or equivalent) checksum of model weights on **every node**, not just the launcher. Verify all checksums match.\n- [ ] Record tokenizer files checksums; verify tokenizer identity across nodes.\n- [ ] Record model config (architecture, dtype, quantization scheme, revision/commit hash if pulled from a registry).\n- [ ] If weights are sharded across nodes (tensor/pipeline parallelism), record the sharding plan hash and verify each node received its expected shard set.\n- [ ] Confirm quantization (if any) is applied identically \u2014 record quantization config hash per node.\n\n### 1.2 Runtime and framework identity\n- [ ] Record framework version (e.g., vLLM, TensorRT-LLM, DeepSpeed, custom runtime) on every node.\n- [ ] Record CUDA/ROCm version, driver version, and NCCL/HCCL/MSCCL communication library version per node.\n- [ ] Record Python environment lockfile hash or container image digest per node. Container digests must match exactly.\n- [ ] Record kernel library versions (FlashAttention, CUTLASS kernels, custom ops) and any JIT-compiled kernel cache state. Note: JIT compilation caches can differ across nodes and silently change numerics \u2014 verify cache proven",
      "reasoning": "",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
